      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism, in its purest form, argues that the Second Amendment guarantees an individual right to bear arms as understood by the Founders, meaning the right is fixed and limited by historical context. Conversely, living constitutionalism allows the meaning of the amendment to evolve with modern society, suggesting the right is a dynamic protection against government overreach. The core tension is whether the amendment is a static historical document or a flexible guide for contemporary rights.",
